## 1. Kali Linux
**Base:** Debian | **Type:** Attack platform (general-purpose)

**Unique feature:** The industry-standard pentest distro â€” successor to BackTrack. Massive community, official certifications (OSCP) built around it, rolling release with constant tool updates.

**Experience:**
- **GUI:** XFCE by default (lightweight, customizable) â€” also offers GNOME/KDE variants
- **CLI:** Central to the workflow â€” most tools are run from terminal, though many have GUI wrappers (e.g., Wireshark, Burp Suite)
- **Friendliness:** Beginner-friendly *documentation-wise* (huge tutorials/community), but the sheer number of tools can overwhelm total newcomers

**Preinstalled tools:** Nmap, Metasploit Framework, Burp Suite (Community), Aircrack-ng, Wireshark, John the Ripper, Hydra, SQLmap, Hashcat â€” 600+ tools organized by category (Info Gathering, Vuln Analysis, Exploitation, etc.)

